10:Done: Both codex dispatches (the T3 linked-cycle on sol, the P4 cljd test-utils on luna) failed on the codex usage limit (resets 23:24 +0700). Re-routed to the available families per routing-status: the T3 architectural diagnosis to kimi k3.1-pro (verified available by test dispatch), the P4 mechanical portability fix to deepseek-v4-pro (verified available). Both re-dispatched and working — kimi is already drafting a tree-depth assertion to replace the fragile pr-str size comparison.\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:619:Done: (1) The T3 linked-cycle round (kimi, re-routed after codex's limit) found the true cause — NOT linked-module wiring: the BUNDLED prelude built a deeply nested linear `then` chain, so `pr-str` recursed past the JVM stack. Fixed by balancing the sequencing at prelude.cljc:4127, with a depth regression test and re-pinned content addresses. Committed c4644d3b. JVM 14/60/0, kondo 0/0. (2) The P4 cljd blocker is deeper than the test-helper require: after removing `yin.vm.test-utils` (e89bb261, which was a real defect too — a test-only namespace in a test's ns form blocking the Dart aggregator), the lane still failed. Isolating by single-namespace compile proves the real defect: `yang.php.antlr.lower` (a src namespace) does not compile on CLJD at all — the compiler reports its whole ns form as faulty with no deeper diagnostic, the same terse shape as the TS prelude overflow. Dispatched to kimi (the same delegate who solved the structurally identical TS case).\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:661:Done: (1) The shiva verification of yang-ts-t3 @ bce0e454: clj 16 ns / 101 tests / 0 failures (765 s), cljd 10 ns / 76 / 0 (683 s) — pass. The cljs tier failed on the known fresh-clone npm gap (@noble/hashes missing); the deps:npm fix + cljs quick + Node slow tier relaunched (tmux t3-node-slow). (2) The p4 lane: the first run's clj tier died on the missing generated ANTLR sources in the