root-cause hypothesis (the \"early exits\" were likely text-mode stream misreads). Re-dispatched EXACTLY per the canonical recipe (fresh session, stream-json): SUCCESS — 38 tool events, full five-section report (12KB, collab/1793214000000-kimi-test-strategy-investigation-r2.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md), session session_b1a13f11-3550-4a81-9a33-ce657a538a31 (captured from ~/.kimi-code/session_index.jsonl). Findings highlight: the selection mechanism is NOT the bottleneck (test:changed:list on yang.clojure.cljc = 1.26s, 61/327 namespaces) — EXECUTION is (unsharded JVM changed lane timed out at 300s); cold prerequisites regenerate ANTLR 3x; wide-change exit-2 is not fail-closed as a workflow. Recommendations: (policy) explicit change-class->gate routing table incl. automatic G3 on wide changes; (mechanics) make SHARDED quick verification the default G2/G3 path (4-6 JVM workers on laptop, remote for lanes predicted >15min, content-keyed artifact caching, warm worktree pool); (structure) retime before re-tiering, medium tier, split mega-suites by contract. Highest-leverage: sharded-by-default G2/G3 execution with automatic wide-change dispatch. Full measured baselines incl. history mining from the old orchestrator log per owner instruction.\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:387:Done: Hardening-2 round 1 delivered and verified. Gate fixtures 4->50 passes on the unchanged 54-fixture baseline (expanded corpus 53/57, 2 genuine upstream failures + host-meta mismatches recorded not normalized); manifest admission inventory sound (155=146+9, 175=165+10 arities, 143 unexercised honestly listed); gensym supply threading verified against upstream rebuild-type; free-vars body verbatim; the real unfold-implicit try shape fits; opacity -> context landed. glm review (session 3ca9258a, two turns: plan-mode analysis then firsthand suites): verdict substantiated, no P0-P2, 4 P3s (stale manifest generator wipes the new schema if run; portable try catches n